  The US Army's Bombardier Global 6500 from
  Leidos (tail number N1098L, callsign AXLE10) is
  a next-generation airborne platform used
  primarily for intelligence, surveillance, and
  reconnaissance (ISR) missions as part of the
  High Accuracy Detection and Exploitation
  System (HADES) program 1 2 3. Its core
  function is to enhance deep sensing capabilities,
  enabling extended-range detection, surveillance,
  and exploitation of threats at high altitudes and
  over long durations 5.
